(load "carp-gametime.carp")

(Project.config "title" "carp-gametime")
(Project.config "docs-directory" "./docs/")
(Project.config "docs-logo" "")
(Project.config "docs-url" "https://github.com/carpentry-org/carp-gametime")
(Project.config "docs-styling" "../style.css")
(Project.config "docs-prelude" "Frame timing for Carp: delta time, time scaling
and FPS.

```
(load \"git@github.com:carpentry-org/carp-gametime@master\")
```

[`Clock`](./Clock.html) is the whole library. It keeps time internally as raw
`Uint64` nanoseconds, so a long session does not accumulate the drift that
summing `Double` seconds would, and it clamps the delta so a frame spike (a
breakpoint, a stalled load) cannot blow up a physics step.

Three deltas come out of one tick, and they are not interchangeable:
`raw-dt` is the wall clock, `clamped-dt` is what the simulation should trust,
and `scaled-dt` is `clamped-dt` times the time scale, which is what gameplay
should use.

```
(let-do [c (Clock.new)]
  (while true
    (do
      (Clock.tick! &c)
      (update-world (Clock.scaled-dt &c))
      (draw (Clock.smooth-fps &c)))))
```")

(save-docs Clock)
; Carp's save-docs hardcodes the index filename as <title>_index.html.
; Rename to docs/index.html.
(defn main []
  (System.system "mv ./docs/carp-gametime_index.html ./docs/index.html"))
